Handling errors in this SDK should largely match your expectations. All operations return a response object or throw an exception.

By default an API error will raise a `{{templateDefaultError true}}` exception, which has the following properties:

| Property       | Type                                    | Description           |
|----------------|-----------------------------------------|-----------------------|
| `$message`     | *string*                                | The error message     |
{{- if eq getResponseFormat "envelope-http" }}
| `$request`     | *?\Psr\Http\Message\RequestInterface*   | The HTTP request      |
| `$response`    | *?\Psr\Http\Message\ResponseInterface * | The HTTP response     |
{{- else}}
| `$statusCode`  | *int*                                   | The HTTP status code  |
| `$rawResponse` | *?\Psr\Http\Message\ResponseInterface*  | The raw HTTP response |
| `$body`        | *string*                                | The response content  |
{{- end}}

When custom error responses are specified for an operation, the SDK may also throw their associated exception. You can refer to respective *Errors* tables in SDK docs for more details on possible exception types for each operation. For example, the `{{sanitizeMethodName .Local.UsageContext.Operation}}` method throws the following exceptions:

{{templateErrorsTable .Local.UsageContext.Operation ""}}

